      "body": "## Why\r\n\r\nPer the convention proposed in #50834, device pointers stored in tensors (`data_ptr()` values) are semantically unsigned 64-bit and should use `torch.uint64` instead of `int64`, which silently overflows/wraps for\r\naddresses `>= 2**63` (observed on XPU USM pointers).\r\n\r\nThis PR only covers `MambaSpecDecodeGPUContext.state_base_addrs` /`block_table_ptrs` in  `vllm/v1/worker/mamba_utils.py`: switch them to `torch.uint64` and drop the `_reinterpret_u64_as_i64` int64 bit-pattern workaround, assigning `data_ptr()` directly.\r\n\r\n## ⚠️ Do not merge until CUDA's pinned torch reaches 2.14\r\n\r\ntorch's element-wise tensor `__setitem__` overflow-checks the assigned Python int as a signed `long long`, even when the target tensor is `torch.uint64` (pytorch/pytorch#191458), so `state_base_addrs[idx] = state.data_ptr()` will raise `\r\nOverflowError:  Python int too large to convert to C long` for real device pointers\r\n`>= 2**63` \r\n\r\ntorch version that doesn't include the upstream fix (pytorch/pytorch#191604, not yet released). XPU has already moved to torch 2.14, which includes the fix, so this works there today; CUDA is still on torch 2.13 and does not have it. Merging now would break Mamba spec-decode on CUDA whenever a state tensor's device pointer happens to\r\nhave its top bit set.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/worker/test_mamba_utils.py` ->\r\n  8 passed, 35 skipped (run on XPU + torch 2.14; **not yet validated on\r\n  CUDA**, blocked on the torch upgrade above)\r\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` on changed files: passed\r\n \r\n",
